sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-charnia-masoni-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Charnia masoni apical Turing wavelength at 140 µm (565 Ma) faithfully reproduces Charnia masoni morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-charnia-masoni-turing-wavelength-s0.py, morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_3145_charnia_masoni_turing_wavelength_s0.lean, datasets/charnia_masoni_turing_wavelength_s0/charnia_masoni_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Charnia masoni specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/charnia_masoni_turing_wavelength_s0/charnia_masoni_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-charnia-masoni-turing-wavelength-s0.py>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_3145_charnia_masoni_turing_wavelength_s0.lean> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-charnia-masoni-turing-wavelength-s0.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_3145_charnia_masoni_turing_wavelength_s0.lean, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/charnia_masoni_turing_wavelength_s0/charnia_masoni_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json; output: docs/media/charnia_masoni_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Charnia masoni; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0, scipy 1.18.1; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability and a critical wavenumber. Schnakenberg 1979: the a - u + u^2 v kinetics integrated here. | Ford 1958 named Charnia masoni. Antcliffe and Brasier 2007 and Brasier, Antcliffe and Liu 2012 describe glide reflection rather than a sea-pen bilateral body. Dunn et al. 2021 argue for apical growth and a stem-eumetazoan affinity. Hoyal Cuthill and Conway Morris 2014 quantify fractal branching.; reconstructed_in_script: Parameters (a, b, D_u, D_v) = (0.14, 0.93, 0.062, 1.35). The determinant-critical wavelength is scaled to 1.404e-4 m. Above onset the fastest mode is longer: analytic λ_m = 167.44 µm. | Explicit-Euler σ(k) versus the eigenvalue formula (Pearson r = 0.9984, RMSE = 0.020). Equal diffusivities give σ_max = -0.900. Scaling both diffusivities moves λ with Pearson r = 1.000 and RMSE 3.26 µm. | A portrait chevron at 58°, the maximum of a four-angle CV probe (48°→87.0, 58°→89.5, 68°→84.5, 78°→83.6). Vertical gradient fraction versus commanded angle has Pearson r = 0.995.; transfer_boundary: The cast is a centimetre-scale relief frond. The chemical wavelength is 140 µm. Only outline, orientation and a stylized chevron cross that gap. The photograph does not resolve 140 µm. | Cohort words 'pigment stripe' and 'ocellus' name the Turing pattern class. The fossil is not evidence of pigment or eyes.; does_not_claim: Does not claim Ediacaran tissue ran these kinetics, or that 140.4 µm was measured on the holotype. | Does not claim a pre-565 Ma chronospecies or a Cambrian successor. The wavenumber ratio to the 6.322 mm organ-scale sibling is 45.03, which is a scale comparison, not a copied parameter set. | Does not generate the higher-order fractal branching of Hoyal Cuthill and Conway Morris 2014. One wavelength is embedded as chevrons. | Nanopublications were not signed. No profile exists at ~/.nanopub/profile.yml.]; phenomenon_size: 126 µm (0.0001264 m, log10=-3.898 m, tier=5_primordium_100um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 126 µm to 28.4 cm): 126 µm:charnia-masoni-bioelectric-polarity, 395 µm:charnia-masoni-vertex-packing, 6.3 mm:charnia-masoni-turing-wavelength, 1.3 cm:charnia-masoni-clock-wavefront, 2.8 cm:charnia-masoni-morphogen-condensation, 3.5 cm:charnia-masoni-elastic-buckling, 4.0 cm:charnia-masoni-flux-canalization, 5.5 cm:charnia-masoni-branching-tree" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1408542111>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1475-4983.2012.01164.x>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/sciadv.abe0291>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1144/0016-76492006-080>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1144/pygs.31.3.211> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/charnia_masoni_turing_wavelength_s0/charnia_masoni_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "datasets/charnia_masoni_turing_wavelength_s0/charnia_masoni_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-charnia-masoni-turing-wavelength-s0.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-delphi10000-charnia-masoni-turing-wavelength-s0.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_3145_charnia_masoni_turing_wavelength_s0.lean> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_3145_charnia_masoni_turing_wavelength_s0.lean" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" .
}

sub:provenance {
    sub:assertion prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1408542111>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1475-4983.2012.01164.x>,
